<title>FRANCE: BNP bought 2.5 mln UAP shares.</title>
<headline>BNP bought 2.5 mln UAP shares.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banque Nationale de Paris (BNP) bought 2.5 million shares in insurance company Union des Assurances de Paris (UAP) on Thursday at 136.09 francs per share, the French stock markets' association SBF said.</p>
<p>The block represents about 0.73 percent in the insurance group which is set to merge with AXA after a share swap bid by the latter.</p>
<p>BNP, already a 17 percent shareholder in UAP, was not immediately available for comment.  </p>
<p>Later, BNP said that the transaction was &quot;pure arbitrage&quot; and had been preceded by the sale of 700,000 AXA shares.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
